// The `names` namespace (area 19, "Registry names"). Its operation is
// listed, typed, in `jadpo-std`'s operation table, which names the Rust
// function in `jadpo-value` that runs it; a test holds this stub to that
// table. It never fails: whether its result is a name the registry takes
// is the registry's to say.

public library names {
    /// `name`, a name in code, as the public registry writes it: lower
    /// case, with a `-` before each capital but the first, so
    /// `AcmeCouriers` is `acme-couriers`.
    function registry_part(name: Text) -> Text {}
}
